 "relevance_note": "A case series of three immunocompromised patients; one, Case 2, is described individually as 'A 17-year-old male with leukocyte adhesion deficiency type 1' (diagnosis only; the paper never mentions ITGB2 or any variant).",
 "method_note": "Hand extraction, no table transcription by script (a script only assembled the JSON). Cases 1 (primary immunodeficiency, T-cell lymphoma) and 3 (severe aplastic anemia) are out of scope and get no rows; cohort size 3. Label 'Case 2' follows the paper's own heading (Table 1 'Case #' value 2 and 'case 2' in the Discussion refer to the same person). No ITGB2 gene name, variant, zygosity or genetic testing is reported, so the variants table is empty and clinical_diagnosis_basis is not reported. n_patients_reported left null because the authors state no number of patients with an ITGB2 variant. Age '17-year-old' is the age at the start of the reported admission (treatment lasted more than eight months); recorded as age at last evaluation as the only stated age. Vital status 'alive' rests on the statement that he was discharged with healed skin grafts (Table 1 outcome 'Wounds healed Pneumonia resolved', no 'Deceased'). 'Non-healing cutaneous ulcers' are not described as necrotic, so 'necrotic skin ulcers or pyoderma gangrenosum-like lesions' is left not reported. Table 1 Scr/CrCl cells and Table 2 MIC cells hold multiple dated values but contain no phenotype information used here. No contradictions found.",
